  "humanObservations": {
    "desktop": "The subagent rows show in the Background tasks pane and as lines in the session output; no teammate row and no shutdown prompt appear. The maintainer could not tell from the UI that the orchestrator agent was acting (a Desktop display gap, not a lifecycle result). The session settings showed bypass permissions as available; every recorded permission mode is acceptEdits.",
    "cli": "Teammate rows, a task list and idle states show as in a team. The maintainer saw late shutdown messages on screen at Stage 3, as the lead reported. The impression that Ava shut down by herself during Stage 1 is not supported by the record: no shutdown request, approval or termination exists before Stage 2, and a message to her was delivered at Stage 2."
  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "summary": "Desktop foreground launches return the report inline in a \"[Subagent hand-back]\" frame with an agent-id footer, not \"Async agent launched\"; the lead's Step 0 text names only the background form, and the lead quoted words the result did not contain. The classification and the behaviour were right.",
      "action": "documented; an optional one-sentence amendment of Step 0 would name the foreground form (it would need a short re-run to be called verified)"
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "summary": "On 2.1.301 a SendMessage to a stopped in-process teammate resumes it with its earlier context (75 and 71 prior messages), so shutting teammates down after the first delivery and revising later loses no context in this scenario.",
      "action": "documented; the lead text about /resume restoring no teammate concerns session resume and stays correct"
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "summary": "The natural late-notice path occurred: four notices (two approvals, two terminations) reached the lead only at the start of its next turn, minutes after the requests; the lead recorded them as evidence and carried on. For the second round none arrived before the end of Stage 4 and the lead said it did not know whether the teammates were still running.",
      "action": "recorded as observed once"
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "summary": "Both lead texts were accurate about shutdown evidence: Desktop never claimed a termination event; CLI separated dispatch, approval and termination and wrote \"not observed\".",
      "action": "none"
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "summary": "The Desktop session ended (SessionEnd) between Stage 2 and Stage 3 and was resumed under the same id; the lead kept its context and continued both finished workers by id afterwards. A SessionEnd in the observer is therefore a session event, not the exit of a worker.",
      "action": "recorded"
    }
  ],
